      <title>Screenshotter 0.11.2</title>
      <pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 12:08:51 GMT</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>0.11.2</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.11.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>https://screenshotter-umber.vercel.app/changelog.html</sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>
      <description><![CDATA[<style>body{font:13px -apple-system,system-ui;line-height:1.45;color:#1d1d1f}h4{font-size:12px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;color:#6e6e73;margin:14px 0 4px}ul{padding-left:18px;margin:0}li{margin:4px 0}code{font:12px ui-monospace,monospace}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f5f5f7}h4{color:#a1a1a6}}</style><h4>Highlights</h4>
<ul>
<li><strong>Screens without a screenshot.</strong> A screen can be just words, stickers and illustrations: it previews, exports as an image or video, and goes in a set like any other. <strong>Just words and doodles</strong> on the start screen begins one; a screen without a screenshot shows a small <strong>Add a screenshot</strong> button instead of asking for one.</li>
<li><strong>Delete pictures you added.</strong> In Images › Your pictures, hover a picture and click its ×, right-click it, or select it and press Delete. If a design uses it you&#39;re told which; <strong>Undo</strong> brings it back.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
